# OpenAPI stays in sync with the routes

`docs/openapi.yaml` is the **source of truth** for this API's contract. It is hand-maintained:
there is no swaggo tooling wired up (no `docs.go`, no `swag` import), so the `// @Summary`
/ `// @Router` godoc comments on handlers are documentation only and generate nothing.

## When this applies

Any time you add, remove, rename, or change the request/response shape of a route
registered in an `api/*/handler.go` `NewHttpHandler` — i.e. any `r.GET`, `r.POST`, `r.PUT`,
`r.DELETE`, `r.PATCH` line. A change is **not complete** until `docs/openapi.yaml` matches.

Update the handler's godoc annotations too, so the two never disagree.

## What to write

Copy the shape of the nearest existing endpoint in the same tag group rather than inventing one.

- `tags:` — use an existing tag from the top-level `tags:` list; add a new one only for a new resource.
- `security: - bearerAuth: []` on everything except `/v1/login*`.
- `requestBody` — `$ref` an existing schema under `components/schemas`. Add a new schema only
  when the Go request struct genuinely has no equivalent yet.
- `responses` — document what the handler **actually returns**, not what would be tidy:
  - `401` from `c.JSON(http.StatusUnauthorized, message)` is a bare `type: string`, not `HTTPError`.
  - `400` / `500` from `utils.NewError(...)` are `$ref: '#/components/schemas/HTTPError'`.
  - File downloads via `c.Attachment` are `type: string, format: binary` under the real
    content type (`text/csv` for CSV, `application/octet-stream` for SAP).
- Path params use `{month}` / `{id}` in YAML, matching echo's `:month` / `:id`.

Do **not** bump `info.version`. This repo has never bumped it when adding endpoints.

## Verify before finishing

Confirm the file parses, every `$ref` resolves, and no route is left undocumented:

```bash
python3 - <<'PY'
import re, yaml, os
doc = yaml.safe_load(open('docs/openapi.yaml'))
documented = {(p.replace('{', ':').replace('}', ''), m.upper())
              for p, ops in doc['paths'].items() for m in ops
              if m in ('get', 'post', 'put', 'delete', 'patch')}
routes = set()
for root, dirs, files in os.walk('api'):
    for f in files:
        if not f.endswith('.go') or f.endswith('_test.go'):
            continue
        src = open(os.path.join(root, f)).read()
        grp = re.findall(r'r\s*=\s*r\.Group\("([^"]+)"\)', src)
        prefix = grp[0] if grp else ''
        for m, p in re.findall(r'r\.(GET|POST|PUT|DELETE|PATCH)\("([^"]*)"', src):
            routes.add(('/v1' + prefix + p, m))
undocumented = sorted(routes - documented)
missing_refs = set(re.findall(r'#/components/schemas/(\w+)', open('docs/openapi.yaml').read())) - set(doc['components']['schemas'])
print('undocumented routes:', undocumented or 'none')
print('unresolved $refs:', missing_refs or 'none')
PY
```

Both lines must print `none`. Then run `make test` per the verification rule.
